  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 128 PM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains in control, though it will gradually slide to \nthe west. This will allow deeper moisture to return to South Texas \nand for a mid-level trough to approach the area. It is possible we \nmay even see a surface reflection of this trough, but it looks very \nweak. Regardless, this will trigger a low (15-25%) chance of showers \nand thunderstorms. \n\nHigh temperatures will continue across the area, with highs in the \nupper 90s along the coast and nearing 105 over the Brush Country. \nHeat index values will 105-109 are expected, though isolated \nlocations could see heat index values around 110.",
